{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_tyylburdgumj4dslvokljxjlq7uvovjfqn5bw7ieoa4mqbqfjxmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte. No divergences found; `translation/src/lib.rs` needed no fixes.**\n\n### Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff | **empty**. C exports 1 symbol (`searchAndReplace`); Rust exports it. 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols. |\n| Phase B — all 24 `CONFIGS.md` rows | **24/24 pass**, ~560 000 randomized differential calls (fixed seeds). |\n| Binary/driver stdout | **N/A** — `CMakeLists.txt` has only `add_library(driver SHARED …)`, no `add_executable`; no `[[bin]]` in Cargo.toml. |\n| Phase C — all 10 `ERRORS.md` rows | **10/10 pass** (13 tests incl. boundary sweeps). |\n| Every feature combination | `cargo metadata` → `[features] == {}`, so one combo; ran all 6 of `{dev, release} × {default, --no-default-features, --all-features}` (profiles differ: `panic=abort` vs unwind + overflow checks). **All green, symbol parity OK in each.** |\n\n### What was built\n- `translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md` — Phase A artifacts.\n- `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` — loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading`, calls only exported `searchAndReplace`; deterministic PRNG; `fork`+`setrlimit(RLIMIT_AS)` and timeout helpers.\n- `tests/valid_paths.rs` (24 tests), `tests/error_paths.rs` (13 tests).\n- `run_all_configs.sh` → `all_configs.log`; `mutation_selfcheck.sh` → `mutation_selfcheck.log`.\n- `Cargo.toml`: added `libloading = \"0.8\"`, `libc = \"0.2\"` to `[dev-dependencies]` (built with `--offline`; the crates.io proxy is blocked in this sandbox, both crates were in the local cache).\n\n### Notable C behaviours confirmed replicated\n- `search == \"\"` ⇒ **non-terminating** loop (`strstr(h,\"\")` returns `h`, `inx_start` never advances). Rust hangs identically; under a capped address space both return `NULL` after unbounded `realloc`.\n- NULL `orig`/`search`/`value` ⇒ **`SIGSEGV`** in both (the C has no null checks; a \"helpful\" Rust null check is caught by the tests).\n- All 5 allocation-failure sites return `NULL` identically, leaks included.\n- `strncpy` NUL-padding and non-overlapping rescan semantics are exact.\n\n### Harness self-check (mutation testing)\nRather than trust green tests, I rebuilt the Rust cdylib 16 times with one injected defect each: **13/13 behaviour-changing mutations were killed**, and **3/3 provably-equivalent mutations survived** (`inx_start2 > from` → `>=` and `from < orig_len` → `<=` add only 0-byte no-ops; the `from > 0` term at lib.c:78 is dead code reachable only via the non-terminating empty-needle path). Proofs are in the script comments.\n\nOne process note: `cargo test` does not build the `cdylib`, so the first all-configs run silently tested the release `.so` under the dev profile. Fixed — the script now builds and pins `RUST_DRIVER_SO` per configuration, and the harness warns loudly on fallback."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":115891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":784,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb637965-6d56-45cb-a0b0-3d71ad74adf0","uuid":"b692ebf7-d14f-4e39-a87f-51b6a1d8b489","timestamp":"2026-09-05T11:28:43.056Z"}
